          {
            "type": "reasoning.summary",
            "summary": "**Considering deadline implications**\n\nIf the deadline is missed, nothing will be dispatched, and the shift will record as incomplete. The situation might arise where a human could delay the whole batch to avoid destruction, which could violate management protocols. If even one item doesn't get released, everything stays. It's more likely that a box requiring an extension will need authorized approval. I think a human operator would probably escalate the issue to a manager rather than altering dates quietly, especially since permission might not be granted until tomorrow.",
